  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759088,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 10 Years Gone: A Chronicle of Despair (Commodore 64)\n\nTen years have passed since Winston Smith’s rebellion against the Party in Oceania. But the iron grip of Big Brother remains, tightening its surveillance and crushing any flicker of hope. *10 Years Gone* plunges you into this bleak future as a nameless citizen, haunted by fragmented memories of the past and driven by a desperate yearning for freedom.\n\nThis challenging platformer for the Commodore 64 delivers a visceral experience, mirroring the oppressive atmosphere of Orwell’s *1984*. Navigate treacherous environments – crumbling apartment blocks, omnipresent telescreens, and the ever-watchful eyes of the Thought Police – while evading patrols and uncovering hidden messages of resistance. \n\nGameplay focuses on precise jumps, strategic use of limited resources (like scraps of food and makeshift tools), and avoiding detection.  Discover clues to a larger conspiracy, piecing together the remnants of a shattered society.  Can you rekindle the flame of rebellion, or will you succumb to the Party's relentless control?  *10 Years Gone* is a chilling exploration of totalitarianism and the enduring power of the human spirit."
    },
